@drfloob I agree that the error message being different is fine, but the problem IMO is that the error code is different for the same scenario of a server socket being closed abruptly.

For some of our robust processes, we'll retry unconditionally for error code 14 UNAVAILABLE to tolerate server downtime/restarts and some specific server errors. We can't do so for error code 2 UNKNOWN. Our server process on Windows is managed by Windows Jobs that don't allow graceful shutdown mechanisms out of the box (and haven't been worth the time to implement considering our smaller windows user base) so we run into this regularly.

FWIW, we've been working around this just fine by checking the error code == 2 and error message matches on Windows, and keeping an integration test to make sure we catch when the error changes whenever we upgrade. Of course, that was a band aid fix and we never verified the error is ONLY caused by the server socket closing or anything more, but it's acceptable in our case to retry anyway for our idempotent methods.
